      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T22:18:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think if there was previously a concurrent map access then there is now a data race on the `closed` field.  There is no synchronization between the writer and the readers, which could be in different goroutines.\n\nFor example, a call to `StartAction` could have finished checking `cp.closed` and moved on to `cp.criticalPath.StartAction` when another goroutines enters `Flush`, updates `cp.closed` too late, and then calls `cp.criticalPath.criticalPath()` concurrently.",
      "revId": "5d63ad61ba501ae4b3659336a70dfb2a10769f10",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a8798dd_bb0edf12",
        "filename": "ui/status/critical_path_logger.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1386891
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T23:43:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought StartAction() FinishAction() Flush() are called from status.go, and status.go has a lock for them. https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/ui/status/status.go;l\u003d283?q\u003d%22FinishAction%22%20s.lock\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main\n\nWe\u0027d better add a lock for critical_path_logger? or is it okay to rely on status.go?",
      "parentUuid": "5378c748_ef2eea35",
      "revId": "5d63ad61ba501ae4b3659336a70dfb2a10769f10",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ccbcf18_f9c6ea9a",
        "filename": "ui/status/critical_path_logger.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-03T05:12:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then where did the concurrent map access come from?  If status.go was holding the lock when it called Flush then StartAction or FinishAction shouldn\u0027t have been able to be called.",
      "parentUuid": "6a8798dd_bb0edf12",
      "revId": "5d63ad61ba501ae4b3659336a70dfb2a10769f10",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8a0e503_c4e4f19b",
        "filename": "ui/status/critical_path_logger.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-03T05:15:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The map read came through metrics, not through status.go:\n```\ngoroutine 1 [running]:\nandroid/soong/ui/status.(*CriticalPath).criticalPath(0xc00028e000)\n\tbuild/soong/ui/status/critical_path.go:109 +0x12b\nandroid/soong/ui/status.(*CriticalPath).WriteToMetrics(0xc00028e000, 0xc00026e000)\n\tbuild/soong/ui/status/critical_path.go:151 +0x95\nmain.main.func2()\n\tbuild/soong/cmd/soong_ui/main.go:223 +0xd5\nmain.main()\n\tbuild/soong/cmd/soong_ui/main.go:231 +0x16d1\n```",
      "parentUuid": "6ccbcf18_f9c6ea9a",
      "revId": "5d63ad61ba501ae4b3659336a70dfb2a10769f10",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "53fae589_15cb4961",
        "filename": "ui/status/critical_path_logger.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1386891
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-03T05:26:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/cmd/soong_ui/main.go;l\u003d228?q\u003ddefer%20%5C(%5C)%20criticalPa%20f:soong\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main\n\n```\n\n\tdefer func() {\n\t\tstat.Finish()\n\t\tcriticalPath.WriteToMetrics(met)\n\t\tmet.Dump(soongMetricsFile)\n\t\tif !config.SkipMetricsUpload() {\n\t\t\tbuild.UploadMetrics(buildCtx, config, c.simpleOutput, buildStarted, metricsFiles...)\n\t\t}\n\t}()\n```\n\nYeah, but stat.Finish() which calls each one\u0027s Flush() is invoked before met.Dump(soongMetricsFile).",
      "parentUuid": "6ccbcf18_f9c6ea9a",
      "revId": "5d63ad61ba501ae4b3659336a70dfb2a10769f10",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5cd464af_5040c53f",
        "filename": "ui/status/critical_path_logger.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-03T05:29:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the problem is deeper in status.go.  The metrics are not written until after `stat.Finish()` has been called, which is documented as:\n```\n// Finish will call Flush on all the outputs, generally flushing or closing all\n// of their outputs. Do not call any other functions on this instance or any\n// associated ToolStatus instances after this has been called.\n```\n\nBut nothing from status.go calls tells the ninja reader goroutine to stop sending data, so if ninja is still running it will happily call the `ToolStatus` methods.  I think when `Finish()` is called it needs to either signal the `ToolStatus` inputs to tell them to stop sending data, or to ignore any further data sent from `ToolStatus` inputs.",
      "parentUuid": "b8a0e503_c4e4f19b",
      "revId": "5d63ad61ba501ae4b3659336a70dfb2a10769f10",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "002f21db_de14d5c9",
        "filename": "ui/status/critical_path_logger.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1386891
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T15:40:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yeah, i agree that we\u0027d better fix the root cause..\n\n\u003e ignore any further data sent from ToolStatus inputs.\n\nfor this, we should add similar logic in status.go instead of here. doesn\u0027t we?",
      "parentUuid": "5cd464af_5040c53f",
      "revId": "5d63ad61ba501ae4b3659336a70dfb2a10769f10",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
